311 0 obj
<<
/Title (As university students, we witness on our own how industry skill demands change in months due to the rapid growth of AI, though academic and TVET syllabuses take years to adapt. Access to high-quality and market-aligned higher education is severely limited by this "curriculum lag" \(SDG 4.3\). As a result, graduates and job seekers enter the workforce with outdated qualifications rather than the relevant technical and professional skills required by current companies \(SDG 4.4\). The entire job ecosystem is affected by the crisis. Without flexible reskilling pathways, working individuals are at risk of displacement, and career centers lack real-time labor market data to successfully mentor students. A negative contradiction is created by this disconnect, causing significant talent shortages in high-growth industries to coexist with rising graduate unemployment and job fragility. The gap negatively impacts full and productive employment by failing to train workers for respectable and durable jobs \(SDG 8.5\). Additionally, ongoing skill gaps hinder workforce productivity and technological innovation, which directly lowers national economic productivity \(SDG 8.2\). Learners are forced to choose between static curricula and an AI-driven economy in the absence of a real-time bridge connecting university education and vocational training to live industry expectations while endangering both individual livelihoods and overall economic growth.)
/Dest [12 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 7 0 R
/Prev 29 0 R
/Next 497 0 R
>>
